      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T18:31:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the first paragraph, I think want something more general here for the labeling model, that touches on these points:\n\n- Resources should have labels even if we aren\u0027t setting them on the backend objects for our memory dumps and other debugging.\n- Resources can change labels over time as they get reused.\n- These changes to the Resource\u0027s label and (if enabled) to its backend label need to be thread safe.\n\nI also think either here or after the 2nd paragraph we should layout how the Resource\u0027s label gets synced with the backend label. I believe the design doc suggested we\u0027d want to set changed labels during `insertRecording` so that we wouldn\u0027t mess with previously set labels for non-shareable/scratch resources in a web capture.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 155,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "88f0c9ad0488cf20260ce821d49ffbba1f447a9a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
