    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28e64806_b199662a",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Resource.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 164,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T18:31:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this can be more summed up like:\n* Any resource can have its label set when it\u0027s first created or inserted into the ResourceCache.\n* Non-shareable resources can also have their label set by the ResourceCache when it returns it from `findOrCreate` (re-adding an initial usage ref).\n* Shareable resource labels shouldn\u0027t change on reuse, so are effectively set once.\n* Scratch resources have complex label management based on their Recorder-local usage (with more details added from the TODO below as it\u0027s implemented).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 164,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "88f0c9ad0488cf20260ce821d49ffbba1f447a9a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab694c0a_17279b98",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Resource.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 164,
